<div class="ms-bar">
  <button type="button" class="solid-btn" id="admAddPartner" data-i18n="adm.addPartner">Add partner</button>
</div>

{#- The thing that was missing, and the reason granting somebody a role did
   not make one appear: a role says what a person may DO, a partner is the
   ministry whose supporters and goals they manage. Sending a new person is
   two acts, and this is the second. -#}
<p class="note">
  <b>A partner is a ministry, not a login.</b> It holds one sent person's
  supporters, goals, milestones and website content. Giving somebody the staff
  role does not create one — you create the partner here and grant them access
  to it.
</p>

<form class="ms-form adm-form" id="admPartnerForm" hidden>
  <div class="ms-grid">
    <label class="fld">
      <span data-i18n="adm.partnerName">Name</span>
      <input type="text" id="admPartnerName" maxlength="200" required
             placeholder="e.g. Chase Roush">
    </label>
    <label class="fld">
      <span data-i18n="adm.partnerFor">Who is it for</span>
      <select id="admPartnerUser"></select>
    </label>
  </div>
  <p class="note-inline" data-i18n="adm.partnerNote">
    Starts as prospective, publishing English only. Add languages and switch it
    to active once there is something to show.
  </p>
  <div class="ms-actions">
    <button type="submit" class="solid-btn" data-i18n="adm.create">Create</button>
    <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="admPartnerCancel" data-i18n="ms.cancel">Cancel</button>
  </div>
</form>

<p class="note">
  A partner's <b>default language</b> is what a visitor to their site sees
  before choosing, and what a translation falls back to when one is missing.
  It is set here rather than in the staff console: there can be several
  administrators, and no public setting should move because somebody changed
  the language of their own screen.
</p>

<div class="adm-partners" id="admPartners">
  <p class="empty" data-i18n="common.loading">Loading…</p>
</div>
